{"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Guides","title":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") makes a struct an event from its declaration. It is a product of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its own that ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" leaves out, so only apps that use it build swift-syntax. It adds","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"BinaryCodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformances, the event’s name, consent category and schema version","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when you give them, and a ","type":"text"},{"code":"schema","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", an ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventSchema","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value that tooling reads:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import EventMacros","","@Event(name: \"checkout_started\", version: 2)","struct CheckoutStarted {","    var cartSize: Int","    var coupon: String?","}","","let tracker = Tracker()","tracker.track(CheckoutStarted(cartSize: 3, coupon: nil))","let properties = CheckoutStarted.schema.properties.map(\\.name)  \/\/ [\"cartSize\", \"coupon\"]"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The schema holds the name, the version, the consent category and each stored property’s name, its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"type as written, its optionality and whether it has a default value, in declaration order. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"encoding writes each of those properties under its name, as a hand-written conformance does","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"), and a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"text":" property keeps its redaction. A record stored before","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a property with a default value (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var currency: String = \"USD\""},{"text":") was added reads it as its default.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"version:"},{"text":" counts breaking changes only, and is 1 when left out; ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents","type":"reference"},{"text":" shows each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"kind of change. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"consent:"},{"text":" sets the event’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"consentCategory"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event(consent: .advertising)"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A stored property whose type isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BinaryCodable"},{"type":"text","text":" is a compile error that names it:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"static method 'requireBinaryCodable(position:)' requires that 'Coordinate' conform to 'BinaryCodable'"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"So are "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":" on anything but a struct, and a stored property without a type annotation. Static"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and computed properties are left out. The struct keeps its memberwise initializer."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Constraining properties","anchor":"Constraining-properties"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A property’s type says what kind of value it holds; a constraint says which values of that kind","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are valid. A rule the type can enforce belongs in the type: a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Refined"},{"text":" value satisfies every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"constraint of its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Refinement"},{"text":" from the moment it is made. Rules a plain ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"text":" can’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"carry are declared beside the property with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Constrained"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"), and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tracker checks them:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["enum CouponCode: Refinement {","    static let constraints: [Constraint<String>] = [.pattern(\"^[A-Z0-9]{6}$\", example: \"SPRING\")]","}","","@Event(name: \"search_performed\")","struct SearchPerformed {","    @Constrained(.minLength(1), .maxLength(200))","    var query: String","    @Constrained(.minimum(0))","    var resultCount: Int","    var coupon: Refined<String, CouponCode>?","}","","let coupon = try? Refined<String, CouponCode>(checked: \"spring\")  \/\/ nil: UnsatisfiedConstraint.pattern","let tracker = Tracker()","tracker.track(SearchPerformed(query: \"\", resultCount: 3, coupon: Refined(\"SPRING\")))","await tracker.finish()","for await report in tracker.rejectionReports {","    print(report)  \/\/ search_performed: \"query\" breaks minLength 1 (1 rejected)","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The keywords are JSON Schema’s: ","type":"text"},{"code":"minLength","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxLength","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (in Unicode scalars) and ","type":"text"},{"code":"pattern","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a string, ","type":"text"},{"code":"minimum","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"maximum","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for a number, ","type":"text"},{"code":"minItems","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxItems","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for an array. Each is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"offered only for the types it applies to, with its bound in the property’s own type, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":".minLength","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or ","type":"text"},{"code":".minimum(0.5)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", is a compile error. In ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Constrained","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so is a lower bound above its upper bound, a pattern that doesn’t compile, and a pattern whose","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"example","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" it, or another keyword of the property, rejects. In a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Refinement","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", those trap when its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"constraints are built. ","type":"text"},{"code":"Refined","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s plain initializer traps on a value that breaks its rule, as an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Array","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" subscript does out of range; ","type":"text"},{"code":"init(checked:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" throws the ","type":"text"},{"code":"UnsatisfiedConstraint","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instead.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Rejected events","anchor":"Rejected-events"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tracker’s worker checks each event’s declared constraints before anything else, never on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"caller. An event that breaks one is rejected: never enriched, held by a consent, written to a store"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or delivered. Each rejection is reported on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tracker.rejectionReports"},{"type":"text","text":" as a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RejectionReport"},{"type":"text","text":" naming"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the event, the property and the keyword, and in debug builds it is logged at error level too."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Unread reports merge, one per event, property and keyword, counting the rejections and the range of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"times they were tracked, so a broken call site in a loop can’t fill memory."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record that a store recovered from an earlier run is checked again, and the store forgets one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that a constraint added since rejects. A stored "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Refined"},{"type":"text","text":" value whose rule no longer accepts it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"doesn’t decode, and the store reports it. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" property takes no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Constrained"},{"type":"text","text":" keywords,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"since checking one would reveal it; a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive<Refined<…>>"},{"type":"text","text":" enforces its rule as it is made."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Both kinds of constraint are part of the event’s schema. The exported tracking plan lists them","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"beside each property’s type, and each example payload satisfies them, using a pattern’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"example"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow"},{"text":"). An array’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Refined"},{"text":" elements are checked as they are made, but their","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rules aren’t exported.","type":"text"}]}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Derive an event’s conformances and schema from its declaration with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":", and constrain which values its properties may hold."}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Defining Events"},"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent\/definingevents"]}],"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://EventMacros/documentation/EventMacros":{"url":"\/documentation\/eventmacros","role":"collection","title":"EventMacros","abstract":[],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/AutomaticTracking":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/automatictracking","role":"article","title":"Automatic Tracking","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Track screen views, control activations and the app’s lifecycle without a call at each place they happen."}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/SessionsAndStandardContext":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/sessionsandstandardcontext","role":"article","title":"Sessions and Standard Context","abstract":[{"text":"Stamp every event with its session and with the app, device, system, locale and network it was tracked on.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/SamplingEvents":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Keep a seeded fraction of the events a tracker tracks, event by event or a whole session at once.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/samplingevents","title":"Sampling Events"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ChangingEvents":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/changingevents","role":"article","title":"Changing an Event","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An event’s version counts the changes that records stored before them can’t be read through, and only those. A compatible change keeps the version; a breaking one raises it."}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent","role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"Vendor-neutral analytics for Swift: typed events, tracked by a tracker and delivered in batches to any number of destinations.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent","title":"Traffluent"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ConsentGating":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Deliver an event only once the user grants the purpose it is collected for.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/consentgating","title":"Consent Gating"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/PersistingRecords":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so a record the app tracked survives the process ending.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","title":"Persisting Records"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TrackingPlanWorkflow":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingplanworkflow","role":"article","title":"Exporting and Checking a Tracking Plan","abstract":[{"text":"Export the JSON Schema of every event an app tracks, commit it, and fail the build when the events stop matching it.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow"}}}